<title>UK: UK GDP rises  0.8 pct in Q3 1996.</title>
<headline>UK GDP rises  0.8 pct in Q3 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following provisional, seasonally adjusted data on Gross Domestic Product (GDP) in the third quarter of 1996. (Index base 1990, constant prices, previous estimates in brackets)</p>
<p>				     Q3,96	   Q2,96	  Q3,95</p>
<p>    Index			  108.9 (108.9) 108.1(108.1) 106.4</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	  0.8   (0.8)   0.5  (0.5)     0.6</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	   2.4   (2.3)   2.1  (2.2)     2.2</p>
<p>IMPLIED GDP DEFLATOR AT FACTOR COST</p>
<p>    Index			  122.5	   121.2	  119.0</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	  1.1	     0.5		0.2</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	   2.9	     2.0		1.5</p>
<p>GDP AT MARKET PRICES (MONEY GDP)</p>
<p>    Index			  134.5	   132.1	  127.6</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	  1.8	     0.9		0.8</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	   5.3	     4.3		4.3</p>
<p>GDP EX OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION (constant prices)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)	  107.8 (107.7) 106.9 (106.9)105.3</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	  0.8   (0.8)   0.4   (0.5)    0.5</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	   2.3   (2.3)   2.0   (2.1)    2.1</p>
<p>OUTPUT DATA</p>
<p>					   INDEX     Q3/Q2    Q396/Q395</p>
<p>    Mining, oil and gas	    142.9     -0.8	  1.8</p>
<p>    Other energy, water supply   121.2     -1.5	  3.3</p>
<p>    Manufacturing sector	   101.9	0.7	 unch</p>
<p>    Total production		 107.0	0.3	  0.5</p>
<p>    Distribution,hotels,catering 107.4	0.2	  2.7</p>
<p>    Total service industries     112.7	0.9	  3.6</p>
<p>GROSS FIXED CAPITAL FORMATION Q3</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/qtr	     -2.2</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/yr ago qtr     3.1</p>
<p>GENERAL GOVT FINAL CONSUMPTION Q3</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/qtr	     1.0</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/yr ago qtr    1.2</p>
<p>CONSUMER SPENDING AT MARKET PRICES</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/qtr	     1.1</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/yr ago qtr    3.3</p>
<p>NOTE - market forecast for the second estimate of third quarter GDP was +0.8 pct qtr/qtr, 2.3 pct yr/yr -- the same as the original figures published on October 25.</p>
</text>
